{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261025T234659Z-fc07633e", "ts": "2026-10-25T23:52:08Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.0-dev", "branch": "fix/1059-skew-note"}, "body": {"base_commit": "b471745d76c4d0d583baaf9cff88c95164d76e9e", "base_tree": "418df10fcf95cda03332baa0cec2b165e27b685a", "head_tree": "d89fc9953bdd711eb381e0c86850a487d730e208", "head_commit": "1b6b92a652fa548ddf950b1b5bc02d5673e673be", "dispatch_commit": "1b6b92a652fa548ddf950b1b5bc02d5673e673be", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "rule-2 cumulative: branch is 5 commits ahead of origin/develop, working tree clean, no fresh cumulative-mode record for current HEAD", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5[1m]"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5[1m]"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5[1m]"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/lib/plan_lifecycle.py", "tests/fixtures/hook_env.py", "tests/test_binary_skew_guard.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md", ".prawduct/changes/skew-note-harness-hooks.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/lib/plan_lifecycle.py", "tests/fixtures/hook_env.py", "tests/test_binary_skew_guard.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md", ".prawduct/changes/skew-note-harness-hooks.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "severity": "note", "title": "Stop/SubagentStop skew silence is keyed on the verb, so an agent running `stop` or `subagent-stop` by hand on a foreign binary now gets no skew note", "recommendation": "Instance. Why it broke: the reporting carve-out keys on the `--session-start` flag, so a bare agent-run `clear` still gets the agent note, but the silence carve-out (`command in _HARNESS_INVOKED_COMMANDS - {reporter}`) keys on the verb alone. That makes an agent-invoked `stop`, whose abandoned-review self-heal writes a fact, silent on a foreign binary. Before this change it got the note. `_check_binary_skew`'s docstring ('Emits on stderr for every agent-invoked command') is false for that caller. No methodology or skill tells an agent to run `stop` or `subagent-stop` by hand (grep of plugin/, documentation/, AGENTS.md found none), so nothing anyone does today goes wrong. Either accept this and make the docstring relational ('every command except the Stop/SubagentStop verbs, whoever invokes them'), or key the silence on something only the harness supplies. No code change is wanted otherwise.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "note", "title": "The sibling pre-dispatch notice keeps the harness-hook channel policy this change just retired for skew", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Why it broke: each pre-dispatch guard decides on its own how it speaks on harness hooks, so the fix reached one of the two. This change rests on two claims: stderr at exit 0 from a hook is only logged, and a note repeated on every Stop is a channel nobody consumes. `_check_ephemeral_worktree` still calls `_print_ephemeral_notice` (stderr) on every proceeding command, harness hooks included. Its docstring says that path is 'the only channel that reaches such an agent without its cooperation', which the new `_SKEW_REPORTING_HOOK` comment contradicts. A session running in a `.claude/worktrees/agent-*` tree gets the fork-point notice on every Stop, which is the same storm, and on SessionStart through stderr, which by this change's own claim the agent never sees. I rated this NOTE rather than WARNING because I could not confirm how often sessions run Stop inside an agent worktree. To close it, give 'how a pre-dispatch notice behaves on a harness hook' one owner, e.g. a helper both guards go through that routes `clear --session-start` to stdout and silences stop/subagent-stop. Or record in the ephemeral guard why its notice is an exception. Search: every `print(..., file=sys.stderr)` reachable before dispatch for a command in `_HARNESS_INVOKED_COMMANDS`.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Shipped comment on _SKEW_REPORTING_HOOK narrates what the hooks used to do", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. This comment explains why Stop and SubagentStop stay quiet: 'they used to repeat the agent-side note ... on every turn \u2014 a channel produced and never consumed, seen as a stop-hook storm.' The reason that holds today, that they fire every turn and no hook can apply the agent-side remedy, is already there. The 'used to' and 'seen as a stop-hook storm' clauses are history, and the change fragment and the test docstrings already keep that history. Delete those clauses and keep the present-tense reason. Prose only: nothing reads it, so the edit is optional.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "warning", "title": "rule-unenforced: the SessionStart skew note says governance writes are guarded, but in a coordinator review the harness consolidates (SubagentStop -> critic_consolidate.consolidate) on the installed plugin, with no guard and now no trace", "recommendation": "Rule: hook-surface.md, \"A docstring or comment is a claim: before one states reach or a guarantee ... grep the callers or test the path\". No deterministic check owns it. Instance: the new SessionStart note is now the only place the skew is reported. It tells the agent that \"Agent-invoked governance writes (`critic-begin`, `critic-consolidate`, `disposition`, ...) are guarded\". The test docstring at test_session_start_reports_the_skew_once_in_hook_words says this guard is \"why the skew is safe to note once rather than on every turn\". But cmd_subagent_stop (prawduct-hook:2645) calls critic_consolidate.consolidate from `_plugin_root()`'s lib. In a framework session started without --plugin-dir, every coordinator-roster review is therefore consolidated, and its fact persisted, by the installed code before the agent can act. Stop's abandoned-review self-heal also writes there. Both are exactly the per-turn writers this change made silent. That is the failure #1059's evidence describes: reviews consolidated by the older -live binary. The fact's `plugin` version cannot tell it apart either, because versions are not the test. What goes wrong: the agent reads the note, concludes foreign consolidation cannot happen, and trusts a review merged by code that is not this checkout's. Instance fix: have the note say that harness hooks, including SubagentStop's Critic consolidation and Stop, write with the installed plugin. That leaves `--plugin-dir` as the remedy for checkout-code consolidation. Mechanizing the class: render the note's guarded and unguarded lists from `_is_data_plane_write` and `_HARNESS_INVOKED_COMMANDS` instead of hand-writing them, and add a test asserting every harness-invoked writer is named. Scope: instance, plus the construction above for the class.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "tests/test_binary_skew_guard.py"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "rule-unenforced: the SessionStart note's lib-skew branch renders a self-contradicting sentence and no test pins it", "recommendation": "Rule: hook-surface.md, \"Prose that REPLACES a deleted control is load-bearing logic: pin every rendered branch, and derive a two-state message from the state\". No check owns it. Instance: in _check_binary_skew's `--session-start` branch, `what` has two values, binary and lib. For kind == \"lib\" the note reads \"this session's hooks are running this repo's script but importing lib/ from ...\" and then \"Hooks always run the installed plugin\". The two sentences contradict each other. The lib case cannot come from the harness, since a hook runs $CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT's own script. It is reachable only when someone runs the repo script by hand with --session-start. test_session_start_reports_the_skew_once_in_hook_words covers only the binary kind. Nothing anyone does changes because of this today. A fix would either word the note from `kind`, or skip the hook wording when kind == \"lib\", which is by definition not a harness call. Mechanizing it would mean parametrizing the session-start test over both skew kinds. Scope: instance.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions for the owner (no plan governs this branch)", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Decisions this branch made, and what settled each. (1) Stop and SubagentStop went fully silent on skew. #1059's proposed change was narrower: route the note to stdout at session start and \"keep stderr everywhere else\". The departure is settled by the change fragment's stop-hook-storm rationale (an unactionable remedy repeated every turn). #1059 was filed by the builder from review R-14, so no owner-stated goal is dropped. Still, the owner sees a different shape than the issue proposed. (2) The carve-out keys on the `--session-start` flag, not the `clear` verb, so an agent's own `clear` keeps the agent note. Pinned by test_agent_invoked_clear_gets_the_agent_note. (3) The hook note drops the `$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT unset` remedy and names `claude --plugin-dir <repo>/plugin`. That is an action only the person can take, yet it is printed on the agent channel with no relay directive. observability-strategy.md \"How the owner actually learns\" names this risk: said to the model, reaching nobody. Whether the agent should relay it is the owner's call. (4) plan_lifecycle drops the `_names` passthrough for direct gitstate.ref_is_branch calls. This is a pure refactor and grep finds no remaining callers. priors: R-4 (rev-20261025T210556Z-91338290, same title, about plan_status/lifecycle decisions) is acknowledged and not re-raised; it covered different decisions.", "files": [".prawduct/changes/skew-note-harness-hooks.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/lib/plan_lifecycle.py"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog item appears resolved: #1059 hook: binary-skew NOTE goes to stderr, SessionStart never injects it", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Both acceptance criteria appear met. `clear --session-start` (and `--brief-only`) prints the note once on stdout. No `--json` command gains it on stdout, because only the session-start call prints to stdout. The change fragment already carries `closes: [brookstalley/prawduct#1059]`. Verify it, then call `/prawduct:backlog update brookstalley/prawduct#1059 status=shipped closed-by=scope:skew-note-harness-hooks` when the backlog skill's \"When to mark shipped\" rule says. Cache age at read: about 350s, no sync_error.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", ".prawduct/changes/skew-note-harness-hooks.md"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "C-B3: open item in the touched area sits next to this work: #563 (guards record no fired event), related to #1059", "recommendation": "Scope: none. #563 \"governance: doctor checks, guards and gates/probes record no fired event\" is #1059's declared `related:` item and stays open; this change does not resolve it. It does move the evidence: harness-invoked skew firings (Stop, SubagentStop) used to leave a log-only stderr line and now leave nothing. Assess and update #563's status. Learnings Cross-Check: the read list was core.md, authoring.md, gates.md, hook-surface.md, release.md and tests.md (from `learnings-files --for-diff`). The change applies core.md's \"A channel that is produced and never consumed is a DEFECT\" rather than regressing it. The two findings above cite the hook-surface rules they rest on. No learnings file changed this cycle, and no implicit supersession was found. Backlog reconciliation used `affecting` (returned #928, not resolved by this change), `search` for skew/SessionStart/stop hook/plugin-dir, and `resolve 1059`.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-8"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 1, "note": 7}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 660, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "pointer-claims-other", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `fix/1059-skew-note`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": "b471745d76c4d0d583baaf9cff88c95164d76e9e", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md", ".prawduct/changes/skew-note-harness-hooks.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-10-25T23:47:03Z"}}

